{{No official name|multi-hit weapons}}
'''Multi-hit weapons''' (also called '''double-hitting weapons'''{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/defender-of-varrock-varlamore-rewards--more?oldschool=1|title=Defender of Varrock, Varlamore Rewards & More|newsdate=31 January 2024|quote='''Double-hitting weapons''' are going to be useful in Perilous Moons}} and '''twin weapons'''{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/varlamore-the-final-dawn-launches-july-23rd?oldschool=1|title=Varlamore The Final Dawn Launches July 23rd!|newsdate=17 June 2025|quote=This is a two-handed '''twin weapon''' requiring 55 Attack to wield.}}) are [[weapons]] that hit an enemy multiple times in one attack. Some weapons attack multiple times on the same [[game tick]] while others attack multiple times on consecutive game ticks.

Multi-hit weapons are useful when fighting NPCs with negative [[flat armour]], such as the [[Blue Moon]], as the flat damage increase gets applied to each hitsplat separately. They can also be useful for delivering killing blows in [[PvP]].

Multi-hit weapons are not to be confused with weapons such as the [[venator bow]] and spells such as [[Ice Barrage]] that hit multiple enemies in one attack, as these are instead considered [[Multicombat area#Area-of-effect attacks|area-of-effect attacks]].

